<item><title>Yogo’s Toubou chiefdom traces more than 125 years of local rule</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/yogo-s-toubou-chiefdom-traces-more-than-125-years-of-local-3f9a0e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/yogo-s-toubou-chiefdom-traces-more-than-125-years-of-local-3f9a0e/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The Niger community near Chad’s border has had five chiefs since its official creation in 1900, with a new leader elected in 2025.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:07:15 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niger reports 81 flood deaths and 131 injured by 31 October</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-reports-81-flood-deaths-and-131-injured-by-31-october-9674cd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-reports-81-flood-deaths-and-131-injured-by-31-october-9674cd/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Floods also affected 97 334 people and destroyed 12 985 homes, according to the population ministry’s representative.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:48:23 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-reports-81-flood-deaths-and-131-injured-by-31-october-9674cd/share.jpg" length="42769" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-reports-81-flood-deaths-and-131-injured-by-31-october-9674cd/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Tiani calls Niger&apos;s consultative council to review two draft laws</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-calls-niger-s-consultative-council-to-review-two-6aff43/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/tiani-calls-niger-s-consultative-council-to-review-two-6aff43/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The council is also due to hear government communications on the expulsion of Mohamids and administrative governance.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:33:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niger opens investor forum with 30 project proposals</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-opens-investor-forum-with-30-project-proposals-f34674/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niger-opens-investor-forum-with-30-project-proposals-f34674/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Prime Minister Ali Mahamane Lamine Zeine said the projects cover agriculture, mining, energy, infrastructure and other sectors.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:53:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Agadez governor thanks religious scholars for prayers for peace in Niger</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governor-thanks-religious-scholars-for-prayers-for-826bdd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/agadez-governor-thanks-religious-scholars-for-prayers-for-826bdd/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Governor Ibra Boulama Issa attended a Quran reading and prayers at Amiskini Mosque, where he relayed thanks from President Abdourahamane Tiani.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:07:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
